# .graphifyignore — extra exclusions for the graphify knowledge graph.
#
# gitignore syntax. graphify reads .gitignore first and this file last, and this
# file can only ever exclude MORE: a `!negation` here cannot re-include something
# .gitignore already dropped. So everything .gitignore covers — SCRAP/, .venv/,
# data/, *.db, __pycache__/, .pytest_cache/, .mypy_cache/, .env* — is already out
# of the corpus and is deliberately not repeated below.
#
# graphify-out/ is also absent on purpose: graphify skips its own output dir
# already, and listing it here risks excluding graphify-out/memory/, which
# graphify always reads back in.
#
# Rule of thumb for adding here: exclude a path if it costs an extraction pass
# but contributes no node worth querying. Do NOT exclude requirements*.txt —
# those mint real dependency nodes the graph uses.

# Local agent state. Classified as "code", yields zero nodes, and rewrites itself
# on every permission change — which re-triggers extraction for nothing.
.claude/

# Packaging metadata with no extractable symbols; emitted a "produced zero nodes"
# warning on the full build.
pyproject.toml

# Scraped HTML debug snapshots (app/config.py: snapshot_dir, default
# "data/snapshots"). The default lives under the gitignored data/, but the path is
# configurable via .env — if it is ever pointed elsewhere, these would be ingested
# as documents and sent to paid semantic extraction. Belt and braces.
snapshots/
*.snapshot.html
how-it-works.html
README.md
TEST_RESULT.md
